  "sourcePath": "contracts/v1/option-question-ergonomics/option-fallbacks.ores",
  "domains": [
    "Option<int>",
    "Result<int,int>"
  ],
  "rules": [
    "Option.unwrap_or_else invokes its zero-argument fallback exactly once only when None.",
    "Option.or_else invokes its zero-argument Option<T> fallback exactly once only when None; returning built-in None keeps the receiver's T.",
    "Option.ok_or evaluates its error argument exactly once on both Some and None, returning Ok(value) or Err(error).",
    "Result.unwrap_or_else invokes its one-argument fallback exactly once only when Err, passing the original error payload.",
    "Result.or_else invokes its callback only for Err and preserves affine receiver ownership; it may not consume a receiver twice.",
    "unwrap and expect panic on failure. Neither trap nor try/catch converts such a panic into a Result/Option.",
    "T? name means Option<T> formal but required presence; T name? denotes independently omittable formal with a checked default if T is not Option.",
    "T? name? carries both properties. Explicit None does not request a default. Postfix expression? propagates None/Err via return, not by throw/panic.",
    "Unlowered parameter omission and postfix expression? remain draft; grammar/tooling tests are not executable backend parity.",
    "All fallback semantics preserve one receiver evaluation and no implicit extra unwrap/flatten of nested Option."
  ],
